# Low Water, Act 2: encounters and their talk exits (Act 2 only; foes are in rules2.lwd). Director's file.

@encounter e.strippers
name: The second low water
area: spit
foe: f.stripper_lead 1
foe: f.stripper 3
param: deck-tilt (the barges lie on their sides)
prop: snare 0 0 ? has(spit.painter_cut)
talk: fx2.strippers.claim | Read them the claim ? (fight_struck >= 1 | fight_seconds >= 10) & fight_lamb_standing >= 4
param: tide-ends-fight
win: spit.fight.strippers.win
yield: spit.fight.strippers.yield
fled: spit.fight.strippers.fled
down: spit.fight.strippers.down

@encounter e.station
name: The Lamplighters' station
area: hill
foe: f.lamplighter 3
param: white-light (no dark anywhere in the room)
prop: cut 0 0 ? has(hill.dark)
talk: fx2.station.tea | Put the pole down and ask for tea ? fight_struck == 0 & fight_seconds >= 5
win: hill.fight.station.win
yield: hill.fight.station.yield
fled: hill.fight.station.fled
down: hill.fight.station.down

@encounter e.zealots
name: Glass heads
area: gasholder
foe: f.zealot 4
param: candles (a knocked candle lights the straw)
prop: lamp 0 0
talk: fx2.zealots.give | Hold the relic up and give it back ? fight_seconds >= 8
win: gasholder.fight.zealots.win
yield: gasholder.fight.zealots.yield
fled: gasholder.fight.zealots.fled
down: gasholder.fight.zealots.down

@encounter e.ice
name: On the ice
area: gut
foe: f.gutter 2
param: ice-floor (both sides slide)
talk: fx2.ice.steward | Call for the steward ? fight_seconds >= 10
win: gut2.fight.ice.win
yield: gut2.fight.ice.yield
fled: gut2.fight.ice.fled
down: gut2.fight.ice.down

@encounter e.substation
name: The second switch
area: hill
foe: f.guard 2
prop: lamp 0 0
talk: fx2.substation.fisk | Let the engineer speak ? has(met.fisk)
win: hill.fight.substation.win
yield: hill.fight.substation.yield
fled: hill.fight.substation.fled
down: hill.fight.substation.down

# Props marked 0 0 are placed by the combat engineer when the spit, hill and gasholder arenas exist
# (the painter as a snare, the substation's white lamp, the altar candles).

@encounter e.strippers.sneak
name: The second low water, from the tarpaulin
area: spit
opening: sneak
foe: f.stripper_lead 1
foe: f.stripper 3
param: deck-tilt (the barges lie on their sides)
param: tide-ends-fight
talk: fx2.strippers.claim | Read them the claim ? (fight_struck >= 1 | fight_seconds >= 10) & fight_lamb_standing >= 4
win: spit.fight.strippers.win
yield: spit.fight.strippers.yield
fled: spit.fight.strippers.fled
down: spit.fight.strippers.down

@node fx2.strippers.claim
place: patience
cost: 2
nar: The assessor takes the claim out of the case and reads it aloud over the barge's tilted rail: Nature of loss, darkness, malicious.
line: SALLIS: Malicious. Then who are we collecting for? {when: !has(cause.wreckers)}
line: LUGG: Malicious. That's us, is it. That's the Company. {when: has(cause.wreckers)}
go: spit.fight.strippers.yield

@node fx2.station.tea
place: station
cost: 2
nar: The assessor puts the pole down on the station's clean floor and asks, in the Shelf's best voice, whether there is tea.
line: GORM: Is there tea? Has the Shelf ever been refused tea in this station? Would it like sugar?
go: hill.fight.station.yield

@node fx2.zealots.give
place: gas_altar
cost: 2
nar: The assessor holds the relic up in the candlelight where every jar can see it, and sets it on the altar step. The glass heads stop. One of them is crying inside its jar, and has nowhere to put it.
go: gasholder.fight.zealots.yield

@node fx2.ice.steward
place: gutter
cost: 1
line: LAMB: Steward!
nar: The word goes up the frozen lane and comes back with somebody large attached to it.
go: gut2.fight.ice.yield

@node fx2.substation.fisk
place: substation
cost: 2
line: FISK: Gentlemen. The specification. Section nine. I wrote it, and I am sorry for the adjectives.
nar: The guards have never been apologised to by a specification. They lower their poles to see what it feels like.
go: hill.fight.substation.yield
